From c098c11d610ec2b6d4bf94859435aa8c3064112f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Martin Lund <mrlund@hotmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 16:01:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 32/35] wifi: ath12k: QMI: WCN7860 firmware download sequence

WCN7860 needs more from the host before it reaches mission mode than
the other chips:

- TME-Lite: the vendor driver hands tmel_peach_20.elf to the firmware,
  by DMA address over QMI (WLFW_TME_LITE_INFO, 0x5B), after target
  capabilities and before board data. A failure is logged and the
  sequence continues, as the vendor driver does.
- M3: the M3 image is phy_ucode20.elf, loaded into DMA memory and
  announced with the usual M3 info request.
- QDSS trace config: qdss_trace_config_v2.cfg is sent after the aux
  ucode (WLFW_QDSS_TRACE_CONFIG_DOWNLOAD, 0x44). A missing file is not
  fatal.
- Regdb: board-2.bin has no regdb for this chip, so a failed regdb
  load does not stop the board data download.
- The cold-boot calibration done indication (0x3E) is handled, so a
  later host capability message reports cal_done.

All of it is keyed on the WCN7860 device id. Other chips take the
existing paths.

The aux ucode is loaded by the existing QCC2072 code, from
WCN7860/hw2.0/aux_ucode.bin (the vendor aux_ucode20.elf).

Assisted-by: Grok
Signed-off-by: Martin Lund <mrlund@hotmail.com>
